{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794292757,"nonce":"tsRFEF0vWbk9HcxwuVFJm1JM7p0=","title":"Enter and Space reach a focused div only as a click; the two cannot be told apart","message":"The window takes Tab, Enter and Space for navigation first (handle_navigation_key). Enter and Space become a click on the focused element and no KEY_DOWN follows, so a widget cannot distinguish Enter from Space. A widget that wants Space to pick up and Enter to open has no way to do it.\n\nEvidence: blinc_app windowed event loop input handling and the offscreen test helper that mirrors it; a key handler on a focused div never sees codes 13 or 32, only on_click with keyboard focus.\n\nExpected: a way for a focused element to receive the raw key (or the key code on the synthesised click).\n\nWorkaround in the caller: treat both as one Activate action.\n\nStand: waits for the Blinc team / fork; no change made here.","files":null}]}